                {
                  "phase": "grammar",
                  "type": "grammar_rule",
                  "content": {
                    "title": "Present simple: I, you, we, they",
                    "explanation": "El present simple describe rutinas, hábitos y cosas que son verdad en general: I get up at seven. Con I, you, we y they el verbo no cambia.\n\nNegativa: don't (do not) + verbo: I don't study. Pregunta: Do + sujeto + verbo: Do you eat together? Respuestas cortas: Yes, we do / No, we don't.\n\nCon palabras interrogativas: What do you do in the evenings?",
                    "table": {
                      "headers": [
                        "",
                        "Afirmativa",
                        "Negativa",
                        "Pregunta"
                      ],
                      "rows": [
                        [
                          "I",
                          "I work",
                          "I don't work",
                          "Do I work?"
                        ],
                        [
                          "you",
                          "you work",
                          "you don't work",
                          "Do you work?"
                        ],
                        [
                          "we",
                          "we work",
                          "we don't work",
                          "Do we work?"
                        ],
                        [
                          "they",
                          "they work",
                          "they don't work",
                          "Do they work?"
                        ]
                      ]
                    },
                    "examples": [
                      "I get up at seven and I go to work by bus.",
                      "We have dinner together on Fridays.",
                      "I don't study. I play video games!",
                      "What do you do in the evenings?"
                    ]
                  }
                },
